      "writtenOn": "2025-05-07T15:44:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`SkPath` is 16 bytes on a 64 bit system (it is more or less a pointer / reference to a `SkPathRef` and a few cached properties) and is generally treated like a value type. At the moment this could consume the ref and it would avoid an extra (though very local) ref/unref pair. At that point it might be worth doing value semantics here (allowing the caller to make the decision) though that will probably end up with a few extra reads/writes on the stack.\n\nExcept that `SkPath` is not currently move-able! This is because of the `std::atomic` members it has. There is an ongoing process to try to fix this (make `SkPath` immutable and introduce a `SkPathBuilder`) but that will take some time. So we could write `std::move` here but at the moment the copy assignment operator is still being called anyway. It\u0027s probably still useful as a marker of intent and means things would work better once `SkPath` is moveable though. But this does currently discourage value type usage here.",
      "parentUuid": "0f124328_23e5df69",
      "revId": "faf0f6c4277b32296a993fd6d2cbaba4b6a7e171",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
